---
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
---

<section id="about" class="scroll-mt-20 px-5 py-20 sm:px-8 sm:py-28">
  <SectionHead index="01" label="Currently" title="What I do" />

  <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.2fr_1fr]">
    <div class="space-y-5 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-mute" data-reveal>
      <p>
        I'm an AI student who would rather ship something real than polish a
        notebook. By day I study Artificial Intelligence in the Honours programme at
        <strong class="text-ink font-medium">VU Amsterdam</strong>; the rest of the time I
        build AI systems people actually use — chatbots and process automation at
        <strong class="text-ink font-medium">Siemens</strong>, and GenAI tools for
        education at the <strong class="text-ink font-medium">VU Education Lab</strong>,
        where I've taught AI literacy workshops to over a hundred faculty members.
      </p>
      <p>
        The common thread: translating a fuzzy "can AI do this?" into a deployed
        answer — scoped, built, evaluated and in the hands of its users. From
        fine-tuning transformers to wiring up OAuth, whatever the gap between idea
        and production happens to be.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="voice-mono space-y-0 self-start" data-reveal>
      {
        [
          ['Siemens NL', 'Working student — AI & Data Science'],
          ['VU Education Lab', 'Student assistant — AI in education'],
          ['AISO × UvA TLC', 'AI Impact Ambassador'],
          ['VU Amsterdam', 'Honours Evaluation Committee'],
        ].map(([org, role]) => (
          <li class="border-line flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b border-dashed py-3.5">
            <span class="text-ink">{org}</span>
            <span class="text-mute normal-case tracking-normal">{role}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
